    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_eafb3564",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: yea_if_you_could_go_ahead_and_explain_memes_that_d_be_great; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in formal attire speaking at a podium, with overlaid text that reads 'yea, if you could go ahead and explain memes that'd be great!'. The scene is a humorous or sarcastic depiction of someone asking for an explanation of memes, likely implying that the person is unfamiliar with internet culture. The overall intent is to create a comedic effect by juxtaposing a serious, formal setting with a casual, internet-savvy request. There is no toxicity present in the image, as it does not target any specific group based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic content. The meme is harmless and intended for entertainment, using the contrast between the formal appearance of the individual and the informal nature of the request to generate humor.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_cc4c2856"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
